It is a fork and is built substantially from the work of others. Attribution,
in order of derivation:

  PlayerEngine — Goodbird-git
  https://github.com/Goodbird-git/PlayerEngine
  LGPL-3.0. The direct upstream. Forked 2026-07-14 at commit
  13fddc140a7ffd60b6bc9d1f084b36adc0674510, re-based 2026-08-22 onto the
  Architectury multiloader tree, and subsequently ported to Minecraft 1.21.11
  by NeoVetta (upstream stopped at 1.21.10). See UPSTREAM_FORK.txt in the
  source repository for the full provenance record.

  Baritone — the Baritone authors
  https://github.com/cabaletta/baritone
  LGPL-3.0. The pathfinding, movement and automation layer, incorporated by
  upstream PlayerEngine. Now located under
  com.player2.playerengine.automaton.* following upstream's package rename
  from baritone.*.

  AltoClef — the AltoClef authors
  https://github.com/gaucho-matrero/AltoClef
  MIT. The task, command and resource-planning framework, incorporated by
  upstream PlayerEngine. Now located under com.player2.playerengine.*
  following upstream's package rename from adris.altoclef.*.

Modifications by NeoVetta are likewise LGPL-3.0-or-later.

This jar is bundled inside the AI Companion mod and is not intended to be
installed on its own.

